  "body": "A Manly classic, tightly held and full of possibility.\r\n\r\nThere is something special about a home that has been cherished for generations, and this 1980s classic is a wonderful example. Positioned on a sought-after, tightly held Manly street, this is an opportunity to secure a property where generous proportions, practical living and a superb setting come together.\r\n\r\nOffering an impressive floor space, the home provides an easy, comfortable layout with room to spread out and enjoy. The generous living room flows through to a separate dining area, while a lovely sunroom opens onto the outdoor deck, creating an inviting space to relax, entertain or simply enjoy the elevated outlook across the tennis courts.\r\n\r\nSet on 793sqm (more or less) of beautifully maintained, manicured grounds, there is plenty of space to enjoy without sacrificing the ease of everyday living.  Inside, you'll find two good-sized bedrooms, excellent storage and comfortable living spaces that retain the character and proportions of their era.\r\n\r\nAdding further versatility is a downstairs studio/granny flat with its own separate entrance. Ideal for extended family, visiting guests, hobbies or working from home, it offers valuable flexibility to suit changing needs.\r\n\r\nCompleting the picture is internal garaging, a workbench and a sought-after location that puts schools, local amenities and the best of the Manly lifestyle within easy reach.\r\n\r\nHomes on this street are rarely available, and with this much floor space, beautifully kept grounds and so many possibilities, this is a property worth your attention.",
